{"title":"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Analytic_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Analytic Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are externally tangent to each other and are internally tangent to a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has a chord that is a common external tangent of the other two circles. Find the square of the length of this chord.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b49c3112557e935af0792920ce28eea2617eab6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.7); size(150); pair A=(0,0), B=(6,0), C=(-3,0), D=C+6*expi(acos(1/3)), F=B+3*expi(acos(1/3)), P=IP(F--F+3*(D-F),CR(A,9)), Q=IP(F--F+3*(F-D),CR(A,9)); D(CR(A,9)); D(CR(B,3)); D(CR(C,6)); D(P--Q); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We label the points as following: the centers of the circles of radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229ef03352b6afcd7e8343bc826c75616d1ff471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d667edd789078808222c08daa5d5f45bbda1723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3,O_6,O_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, and the endpoints of the chord are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d559f1ae366d6c7ddffa20b504ac135a430839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84ca528a796a9b12d98428a14f0c955ad0fa64a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3,A_6,A_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> be the feet of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendiculars</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d667edd789078808222c08daa5d5f45bbda1723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3,O_6,O_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" /> (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a5c65861ea866ea159f86a1136df0bca4b10cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3,A_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> are the points of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent_(geometry)\" title=\"Tangent (geometry)\">tangency</a>). Then we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356119b17296ab123f99f0cda8cf46d5e561cd45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{O_3A_3} \\parallel \\overline{O_6A_6} \\parallel \\overline{O_9A_9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/139a16fc6e4c52031c2a162eb9eaf36f13fc66ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_6O_9 : O_9O_3 = 3:6 = 1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed0195cfb6c122d23e82f1001aa911317c3dced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_9A_9 = \\frac{2 \\cdot O_6A_6 + 1 \\cdot O_3A_3}{3} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"255\" height=\"38\" /> (consider similar triangles). Applying the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3cf054308cec2d5c89324e6e9353695b0b4cda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle O_9A_9P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />, we find that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488622eb2717ff4167da99192b30263d4432c7ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PQ^2 = 4(A_9P)^2 = 4[(O_9P)^2-(O_9A_9)^2] = 4[9^2-5^2] = \\boxed{224}\\]\" width=\"474\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48be03ee754e516e7858ae5ff4b144b4d32e4cf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.7); size(150); pair A=(0,0), B=(6,0), C=(-3,0), D=C+6*expi(acos(1/3)), F=B+3*expi(acos(1/3)),G=5*expi(acos(1/3)), P=IP(F--F+3*(D-F),CR(A,9)), Q=IP(F--F+3*(F-D),CR(A,9)); D(CR(D(MP(&quot;O_9&quot;,A)),9)); D(CR(D(MP(&quot;O_3&quot;,B)),3)); D(CR(D(MP(&quot;O_6&quot;,C)),6)); D(MP(&quot;P&quot;,P,NW)--MP(&quot;Q&quot;,Q,NE)); D((-9,0)--(9,0));  D(A--MP(&quot;A_9&quot;,G,N)); D(B--MP(&quot;A_3&quot;,F,N)); D(C--MP(&quot;A_6&quot;,D,N)); D(A--P); D(rightanglemark(A,G,P,12)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" /></center>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Analytic_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Analytic_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Analytic Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Analytic Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2ba3edd7981fa26cb04db42091fc4f1dd9ad3a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.7); size(150); pair A=(0,0), B=(6,0), C=(-3,0), D=C+6*expi(acos(1/3)), F=B+3*expi(acos(1/3)),G=5*expi(acos(1/3)), P=IP(F--F+3*(D-F),CR(A,9)), Q=IP(F--F+3*(F-D),CR(A,9)); D(CR(D(MP(&quot;E&quot;,A)),9)); D(CR(D(MP(&quot;F&quot;,B)),3)); D(CR(D(MP(&quot;D&quot;,C)),6)); D((-9,0)--(9,0)); D(MP(&quot;&quot;,P,NW)--MP(&quot;&quot;,Q,NE)); D(A--MP(&quot;B&quot;,G,N)); D(B--MP(&quot;C&quot;,F,N)); D(C--MP(&quot;A&quot;,D,N)); D(rightanglemark(A,G,P,12)); D(rightanglemark(C,D,P,12)); D(rightanglemark(B,F,P,12)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be defined as the origin of a coordinate plane with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis running across the chord and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da924c82a3296c56c076eacbd295f801a2652c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(6\\sqrt{2},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"24\" /> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c995b3a0c553c7bc6860bb663badd03ed10150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(0,-6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060b3db0a2a91dd52bb0c894b3857804bbcc2992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(6\\sqrt{2},-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"24\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f519641e2ba6f36cb90fd1dc4c4ec0b9cc747f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DE}{DF}=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"39\" />, the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is one-third of the way from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, so point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f1c729d45befad4e2415c9c4310ae2465c7f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\sqrt{2},-5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"24\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the equation of this circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba1d6a032a5f492467c7e1806c3009df4c258eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2\\sqrt{2})^2+(y+5)^2=81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"24\" />. Since the chord's equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we must find all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the equation of the circle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5984cdea0f67cecb8983324088523a8dbe7c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-2\\sqrt{2}=\\pm\\sqrt{56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />, so the chord has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa54bfbeeb883192b9bf248067637fd8c6550dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\sqrt{56}+2\\sqrt{2}-(-\\sqrt{56}+2\\sqrt{2})|=2\\sqrt{56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"307\" height=\"24\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41cacea5bd2a141568058e7a91e5ce4e4d5637b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\sqrt{56})^2=\\boxed{224}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"129\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For more practice, try 2005 AIME II #8. The idea is identical and it is just more work. \n</p><p>~Aarav22\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar problem for extra practice: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME\" title=\"1995 AIME\">1995 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185034\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.727 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 278/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8440/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.292      1 -total\n 60.05%    7.982      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.37%    4.967      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2974:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185034 and revision id 287257. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}